most powerful feature – Pipelines (Jenkinsfile).

🔹 A Pipeline is the automated flow of steps from code → build → test → deploy.
🔹 It is written in a file called Jenkinsfile, stored in the project repo.
🔹 Two ways to write pipelines:

Declarative Pipeline → simple & structured (best for most use cases).

Scripted Pipeline → flexible, uses Groovy for complex cases.


👉 Why is it important?

Pipelines = CI/CD as Code.

Version-controlled → easy to track changes.

Reusable & portable → same pipeline works across environments.
